cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite the versioned software release."
title: "Genuine Zero Uniform Atlas Energy"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Massensini
    given-names: Thiago
license: MIT
version: 0.13.0
date-released: 2026-08-18
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 formalization of the native real-camera/Genuine zero identity, the
  faithful C2--C7 cutoff operator, exact critical cutoff-tail jets, and the
  finite-to-limit transverse-energy architecture. Version 0.13.0 adds a
  kernel-checked microscopic coercivity bridge: exact moving-clock
  reoptimization, primitive quotient estimates, and concrete six-camera
  residual, corrected first-jet, pairing, energy, and Schur-coefficient
  reductions. The release removes the historical phase-floor-greater-than-four
  threshold from the abstract eventual-positivity step. It does not promote
  the remaining uniform finite-jet bounds, denominator floors, compact-region
  coverage, numerical evidence, or readout-domain equivalences to an
  unconditional confinement theorem.
